# This repo holds agent definitions, skills and suites — not a build.
# `nawi` is a separate repository with its own .gitignore; the build
# outputs it produces (out/, release/, test-results/) are ignored there, not
# here, so this file no longer duplicates them.

# --- nawi ------------------------------------------------------------
# It was recorded as a gitlink (mode 160000) with no .gitmodules and no remote,
# so cloning this repo produced an empty, unpopulatable directory. It is a
# genuinely separate project — its own history, its own branches — that these
# agents build against, not a component of this one. Untracked deliberately:
# `git rm --cached nawi`. Its repository is intact on disk.
nawi
# Same directory, pre-rename name — until the rename lands, both must be ignored.
snagit-clone/

# --- Agent runtime artifacts -------------------------------------------------
# Worktrees created by the Workflow tool for isolated agent builds. They are
# real checkouts and must never be committed into the parent.
.claude/worktrees/
**/.claude/worktrees/

# Transcripts, task output and scratch space written during agent runs.
.claude/tasks/
.claude/scratchpad/
.claude/shell-snapshots/
.claude/statsig/
.claude/todos/

# Agent definitions, skills, plugins and project memory under .claude/ ARE the
# point of this repo — do not add a blanket `.claude/` rule here.

# --- Local machine state, never shared ---------------------------------------
# Per-machine overrides. These routinely hold absolute paths, machine-specific
# permission grants and occasionally tokens — none of it meaningful to anyone
# else, and some of it not safe to publish.
**/settings.local.json
**/*.local.json
.claude/projects/
.claude/history.jsonl
.claude/ide/
.claude/plugins/repos/

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository is public. Nothing below should ever be in it, and an
# allowlist that nothing reads is worse than none — see the Nawi repo for how
# that went.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.secrets
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
**/mcp-config.json

# --- Tooling -----------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- OS and editor -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

# --- Machine-local harness state -------------------------------------------
# settings.json is per-machine for every harness, not only the .local.json form.
# The rule above (`**/*.local.json`) was written for a filename that is not the
# one in use, so .commandcode/settings.json was tracked and published one
# machine's absolute paths, a stale pid, and a wildcard shell allowlist.
.commandcode/settings.json
.commandcode/taste/
**/settings.json
!.vscode/settings.json

# --- Sibling worktrees and separate projects --------------------------------
# nawi-vex is a git worktree of the nawi repo. The bare `nawi` rule above does
# not match it, so one `git add -A` would have committed a second project
# including its node_modules/ and a 265 KB lockfile.
nawi*/

# --- Run state ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-run recorder output. Transient, per-machine, and regenerated every run.
.claude/runs/

# --- Learning loop instance data ---------------------------------------------
# The denylist is instance data: it names this adopter's organisations,
# projects and customers. Quarantine holds candidates that matched a redaction
# class and must never be committed.
redaction/denylist.txt
learnings/quarantine/

# --- Python build output ----------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
